 # sibling entities (humidity / CO2 / battery — attributes that fluctuate), so
 # a stable-but-alive room keeps publishing while a dead device still goes
 # all-attributes-silent and is dropped inside the same 45-min threshold.
+#
+# PER-ROOM LIVENESS MODE (2026-08-22, SlyTherm#192). Report-age gating turned
+# out to be the wrong instrument for the two ZHA rooms. Over 10 days the gate
+# was hot 65.6% of minutes and produced 48 of the 51 phone pushes in 48 h,
+# flapping offline→OK every ~55 min, while ZHA logged ZERO unavailable events
+# across all 97 entities and the Zigbee coordinator never reset. Dining Room's
+# worst gap between value-changes on ANY sibling was 801.7 min — longer than
+# ZHA's own 6 h battery timeout, i.e. the device was demonstrably in radio
+# contact for 13.4 h while this guard counted it silent. No reachable slider
+# value could fix that (the helper's ceiling was 240).
+#
+# So each room now declares HOW it is judged, via `liveness:` in the roster:
+#   report        (default) freshest last_reported across `live` siblings,
+#                 compared to input_number.slytherm_sensor_stale_min. Right for
+#                 the cloud-backed rooms, where a wedged cloud can serve frozen
+#                 data from a dead device — the 2026-07-27 failure mode.
+#   availability  the integration's own availability check is the liveness
+#                 signal: alive unless the temp entity is unavailable/unknown.
+#                 Right for ZHA end devices, which have no cloud cache to
+#                 freeze behind — when they die they go unavailable.
+# Trade-off accepted knowingly (owner decision 2026-08-22): a genuinely dead
+# SNZB-02D now keeps feeding fusion until ZHA marks it unavailable
+# (consider_unavailable_battery, 6 h default) instead of stale_min. That is
+# slower than 45 min but faster than the only threshold that would have
+# silenced the false alarms (~900 min), so it beats the alternative on both
+# axes. Do NOT lower consider_unavailable_battery to compensate without first
+# measuring the devices' real check-in cadence — setting it below that
+# reintroduces exactly this flapping.
 
