+  # `liveness: availability` in the roster ignore it (see the header note).
+  # Tune from sensor.slytherm_stale_room_sensors' `ages` attribute: set it
+  # comfortably above the worst age a HEALTHY sensor reaches, or the bridge
+  # will drop good rooms. Measured over 10 days: Living Room max 34.7 min,
+  # Basement max 383.9 min (Basement is currently participating=off).
+  #
+  # NO `initial:` — deliberately (SlyTherm#192). For input_number, a defined
+  # `initial:` OVERRIDES state restoration, so HA forced this helper back to 45
+  # on every restart and silently reverted kazoo-home-assistant#4's set_value
+  # to 180. The recorder showed it plainly: every write in a 10-day window was
+  # 45.0 and every one landed at an HA start event. Without `initial:` the
+  # helper restores its last value across restarts; on a fresh install it comes
+  # up unknown and all three consumers (the bridge condition and the two
+  # template blocks below — verified 2026-08-22, nothing outside this file
+  # reads the helper) fall back to `| float(45)`, i.e. exactly
+  # today's behaviour. Set the value once via input_number.set_value — editing
+  # this block alone does NOT change the restored value.
   slytherm_sensor_stale_min:
     name: SlyTherm room sensor stale after
     min: 5
-    max: 240
+    max: 1440   # was 240: below Dining's real tail, so no slider value worked
