 # zigbee_sensors.yaml — availability alerts for the Zigbee (ZHA) room sensors.
 #
-# Both SONOFF SNZB-02D temp/humidity sensors talk directly to the ZHA
-# coordinator (SONOFF ZBDongle-E on kdocker2) — no Zigbee routers in the mesh
-# yet, so a dropped end device can't rejoin on its own. This package alerts
-# when a sensor goes unavailable so you can re-pair it (ZHA "Add device" +
-# ~5 s long-press on the sensor) instead of silently losing data.
+# Both SONOFF SNZB-02D temp/humidity sensors report to the ZHA coordinator
+# (SONOFF ZBDongle-E on kdocker2). This package alerts when a sensor goes
+# unavailable so you can re-pair it (ZHA "Add device" + ~5 s long-press on the
+# sensor) instead of silently losing data.
+#
+# MESH (corrected 2026-08-22, SlyTherm#192 §5d — this header used to say there
+# were no routers and to go buy one; there are two). Both Third Reality night
+# lights are mains-powered ZHA routers (logical_type 1), and both SNZB-02Ds are
+# parented through them — Dining Room at LQI 84 on the 2026-08-22 sweep. The
+# mesh has been clean: 0 unavailable events across all 97 ZHA entities in 10
+# days, and 0 USB re-enumerations of the coordinator in 12 days. No hardware
+# needed.
 #
 # NOTE on timing: ZHA only marks a *battery* device unavailable after a ~6 h
 # "not seen" timeout (consider_unavailable_battery), so these alerts land a few
-# hours after a real dropout — reliable, not instant. A mains-powered Zigbee
-# router near the sensors would cut dropouts and speed detection.
+# hours after a real dropout — reliable, not instant.
+#
+# THIS IS NOW LOAD-BEARING (SlyTherm#192). The two ZHA rooms carry
+# `liveness: availability` in slytherm_sensors.yaml, so ZHA's availability
+# check — not report-age — is what gates them out of the thermostat's fusion.
+# A dead SNZB-02D therefore surfaces on the ~6 h timeout above, here and there
+# at once. Tempting knob, real trap: do NOT lower consider_unavailable_battery
+# to speed that up without first measuring these devices' true check-in cadence
+# (device last_seen, which advances on any received frame — NOT the value-change
+# age visible in the recorder). Set below the real cadence and both alerts flap,
+# which is the failure #192 fixed.
 #
 # Entities (from ZHA; auto-created, not defined here):
 #   sensor.sonoff_snzb_02d_temperature      Dining Room
